-- miscellaneous.l4 — Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 (Cth),
-- Part 4 (ss 14–16), and the entry points that put the Bill together.
--
-- Source: ../../sources/26S2721.txt. "ISSUE n" points into ISSUES.md.

IMPORT support
IMPORT definitions
IMPORT `selection-process`

§ `Part 4 — Miscellaneous`

§§ `s 15 — Appointments to which this Act applies`

-- "This Act applies in relation [to] an appointment made on or after the
-- commencement of this section if the term of the appointment starts at least
-- 12 months after that commencement." The missing "to" is ISSUE 20. What the
-- "term" of a head-of-mission appointment is, and when it "starts", is ISSUE 17.
-- s 15 speaks only of appointments; whether it also limits s 11 and s 14(4)-(6)
-- (acting arrangements) is ISSUE 18. This encoding applies it to appointments
-- only.
@ref Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 s 15, s 2
GIVEN `the case`               IS AN `Appointment case`
      `the day of Royal Assent` IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15 — this Act applies to the appointment in` `the case` `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` MEANS
        "made on or after the commencement of this section"
    ... (commencement `is on or before` (`the case`'s `the day the appointment is made`))
    AND "the term of the appointment starts at least 12 months after that commencement"
    ... ((commencement `plus calendar months` 12) `is on or before` (`the case`'s `the day the term of the appointment starts`))
    WHERE
        commencement MEANS `s 2 — the day this Act commences, given` `the day of Royal Assent`

§§ `s 14 — Overarching prohibition and consequences of noncompliance`

-- s 14(1): "must not be made otherwise than in accordance with this Act".
-- Narrow reading (operative here): the conditions on which s 9(1) makes the
-- appointment permissible. The broad reading also asks whether the procedure
-- that produced a s 9(2) recommendation was followed (the list, its timing,
-- the Committee's size, the notice's timing, the candidate being on the list).
-- Which one triggers the duty to terminate in s 14(3) is ISSUE 16.
GIVEN `the case`      IS AN `Appointment case`
      `the Committee` IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the procedure behind the Committee's recommendation was followed, in` `the case` `the Committee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Committee`'s `the candidate list`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST l  THEN
            `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `the Committee` l
        AND `s 12(3) — the Committee consists of 3 members` `the Committee`
        AND `s 10(3) — the Committee gave its written notice in time` `the Committee`
        AND `at least one of` (l's `the proposed candidates`) `satisfies` isTheAppointee
    WHERE
        isTheAppointee c MEANS c's `the person`'s `name` EQUALS `the case`'s `the appointee`'s `name`

GIVEN `the case` IS AN `Appointment case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) — broad reading: the appointment is in accordance with this Act` `the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` `the case` EQUALS `no route under section 9`
            THEN FALSE
        IF `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` `the case` EQUALS `s 9(2) — on a Selection Committee's recommendation`
            THEN `at least one of` (`the case`'s `the Selection Committees established for an appointment to the office`) `satisfies` recommendedProperly
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHERE
        recommendedProperly c MEANS
                (`the Committee's recommendation is still in effect for` `the case` c)
            AND (`the Committee had given notice of` (`recommending the appointment of` (`the case`'s `the appointee`'s `name`)) `by the appointment in` `the case` c)
            AND (`the procedure behind the Committee's recommendation was followed, in` `the case` c)

DECLARE `Status of the appointment` IS ONE OF
    `the office is not a designated diplomatic office (s 7), so this Act does not govern the appointment`
    `this Act does not apply to the appointment (s 15)`
    `the appointment may be made on a Selection Committee's recommendation (s 9(2))`
    `the appointment may be made after two referrals because the Minister is satisfied (s 9(3)(c)(i)); the Minister must table a statement of reasons in each House within 5 sitting days (s 9(4)-(5))`
    `the appointment may be made after two referrals with the approval of both Houses (s 9(3)(c)(ii))`
    `the appointment must not be made (s 14(1)); if made it is valid (s 14(2)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(3))`

@export Decide whether, and by which route, an appointment to an Australian diplomatic office may be made under the Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026, and what follows if it may not
GIVEN `the case`               IS AN `Appointment case`    @desc The appointment: the office, the appointee and their political history, the dates, every Selection Committee established for an appointment to the office, the days of earlier appointments to it, and the s 9(3)(c) facts
      `the day of Royal Assent` IS A `Calendar date`       @desc The day the Act receives the Royal Assent; it commences the next day (s 2)
GIVETH A `Status of the appointment`
`the status of the appointment in` `the case` `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` (`the case`'s `the office`)
            THEN `the office is not a designated diplomatic office (s 7), so this Act does not govern the appointment`
        IF NOT `s 15 — this Act applies to the appointment in` `the case` `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent`
            THEN `this Act does not apply to the appointment (s 15)`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` `the case`
            WHEN `s 9(2) — on a Selection Committee's recommendation`
                THEN `the appointment may be made on a Selection Committee's recommendation (s 9(2))`
            WHEN `s 9(3)(c)(i) — after two referrals, the Minister being satisfied`
                THEN `the appointment may be made after two referrals because the Minister is satisfied (s 9(3)(c)(i)); the Minister must table a statement of reasons in each House within 5 sitting days (s 9(4)-(5))`
            WHEN `s 9(3)(c)(ii) — after two referrals, with the approval of both Houses`
                THEN `the appointment may be made after two referrals with the approval of both Houses (s 9(3)(c)(ii))`
            WHEN `no route under section 9`
                THEN `the appointment must not be made (s 14(1)); if made it is valid (s 14(2)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(3))`

DECLARE `Status of the acting arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `the office is not a designated diplomatic office (s 7), so this Act does not govern the arrangement`
    `the arrangement may be made (s 11)`
    `the arrangement must not be made (s 14(4)); if made it is valid (s 14(5)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(6))`

@export Decide whether a person may act in an Australian designated diplomatic office (as chargé d'affaires) under section 11 of the Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026
GIVEN `the arrangement` IS AN `Acting arrangement` @desc The acting arrangement: the office, the person who is to act and their political history, the day it is made, and why the office needs someone to act
GIVETH A `Status of the acting arrangement`
`the status of the acting arrangement` `the arrangement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` (`the arrangement`'s `the office`)
            THEN `the office is not a designated diplomatic office (s 7), so this Act does not govern the arrangement`
        IF `s 11(2) — the chargé d'affaires may act` `the arrangement`
            THEN `the arrangement may be made (s 11)`
        OTHERWISE `the arrangement must not be made (s 14(4)); if made it is valid (s 14(5)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(6))`

-- s 14(3) and (6): the duty to terminate. "as soon as practicable after the
-- Minister becomes aware" sets no number, so there is no WITHIN: the duty is
-- outstanding until performed and is never breached by the clock alone. The
-- sentence is passive and names no one who must terminate: ISSUE 5.
-- Clock: days, starting the day the Minister becomes aware.
@ref Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 s 14(3)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor` `Act under this Bill`
`s 14(3) — the duty to terminate a noncompliant appointment` MEANS
    PARTY `the person who makes the appointment or arrangement`
    MUST  `terminate the appointment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the person who makes the appointment or arrangement` BECAUSE "s 14(3): appointment made otherwise than in accordance with the Act not terminated as soon as practicable"

@ref Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 s 14(6)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor` `Act under this Bill`
`s 14(6) — the duty to terminate a noncompliant acting arrangement` MEANS
    PARTY `the person who makes the appointment or arrangement`
    MUST  `terminate the arrangement`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the person who makes the appointment or arrangement` BECAUSE "s 14(6): acting arrangement made otherwise than in accordance with the Act not terminated as soon as practicable"

-- s 14(7): the Commonwealth's other powers to terminate are not limited.
-- Nothing reads it.

§§ `s 16 — Rules`

-- The Minister may make rules by legislative instrument. The only
-- "prescribed by the rules" hook in the Bill is s 7(2), carried as the input
-- `prescribed by the rules` on `another office of the Commonwealth`.
-- s 16(2): the rules may not create an offence or civil penalty, provide
-- arrest/detention or entry/search/seizure powers, impose a tax, or directly
-- amend the Act. Nothing here reads it.
